    "b-ks2-path-run-intro": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The attempt pathway uses "
        },
        {
          "insert": "index_task.pathway",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "run_closed",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". It fires when a worker run closes. The worker summary agent runs once, from a single prompt, and writes the run object, consisting of the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row and its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "submission",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows with hypothesis, scored tries, and outcomes. It then enqueues an attempt index task. It summarizes and proposes; it never writes a fact. The librarian decides whether anything the run learned changes what is on the page."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-run-agents-heading": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-agents-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Agents Called"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-run-agents-table": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-agents-table",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Order",
          "Agent",
          "Does"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "1",
            "Worker summary agent",
            [
              {
                "insert": "At run close, from a single prompt: writes the "
              },
              {
                "insert": "worker_run",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " row and its "
              },
              {
                "insert": "submission",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " rows plus a fact proposal, advances the "
              },
              {
                "insert": "attempt",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " watermark, enqueues the index task. Never writes facts"
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            "2",
            "Librarian",
            [
              {
                "insert": "Consumes the task: reads the run object and the proposal, decides per touched target or entity whether the facts change, searches the sources for corroboration, overwrites live "
              },
              {
                "insert": "fact",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " rows with "
              },
              {
                "insert": "attempt://",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " citations"
              }
            ]
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-run-conflict": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-conflict",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "After close, integration either lands with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run.integration",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "integrated",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", or conflicts because upstream moved or another worker's merge landed first on the file. No agent resolves the conflict: the run-loop records it deterministically on the run row as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "integration",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "conflicted",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "integration_detail",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "{ status, disposition, conflict_paths[], failure_reasons[], resolved_at }",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", derived from run state's integration rows. It re-queues the target for the next epoch; the next worker sees the conflicted run with its conflict paths (capped at 10) on its card."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-run-conflict-detail-1": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-conflict-detail-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The summary agent runs in both cases, with the integration record as narrative input, so the knowledge is not wasted. There is no regression event and no extra pathway; what the run learned reaches the graph through this pass."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-run-drift": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-drift",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The "
        },
        {
          "insert": "run_closed",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " context carries, per touched subject, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "renamed_from",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " with the stable keys of rows whose "
        },
        {
          "insert": "moved_to_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " points at it, written by report reconciliation when the checkout head moved. It also carries the flagger's compact drift report over its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "code://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " citations (unchanged | drifted | unresolvable). The pass is drift-gated: after apply the flagger re-runs on the touched subjects. A clean result completes the pass; drift left releases the task once for a retry; drift left again completes with the warning recorded in the pass artifact. See "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Drift Gate",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/20-knowledge-base/40-librarian-pathways/50-drift-gate",
              "label": "Drift Gate"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-run-librarian-heading": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-librarian-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Librarian Operation"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-run-librarian-reads": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-librarian-reads",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The librarian reads the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row, its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "submission",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows, and the proposal, alongside the live "
        },
        {
          "insert": "fact",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows for "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run.target_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The run's target is the subject first; a submission that leaned on a struct, a field, or a neighbouring function puts that entity's facts in scope too. Only the librarian searches the sources. The structured attempts query (target, outcome, score trajectory) is the first query, keyword over hypotheses and transcripts follows, the code graph checks a claim against the checkout, and archival keyword and vector search corroborate when the run's claims echo something Discord, a PR, or the wiki already said."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-run-librarian-writes": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-librarian-writes",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Every write goes through the resolver. The affected live "
        },
        {
          "insert": "fact",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows are overwritten in place, each fact's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evidence",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows replaced wholesale with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "attempt://run/<worker_run.id>[/submission/<seq>]",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " locators into the run and its scored tries, plus whatever corroboration the search returned. A run outcome never becomes a fact by itself, and a tested hypothesis that failed stays on the ledger side, citable later as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "attempt://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " evidence. A resolution move that keeps recurring across runs may be filed as a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pattern",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " fact. The "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pattern",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " entity is curated, and the librarian is its only writer."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
